Based on the new spec (Aug 30) every Link should render as an “inline” link by default (i.e. with an underline) and allow turning that off via a prop. Currently our `<Link>` never emits the modifier class and so you cannot style “inline” vs “stand-alone” links. Below patch adds:

- a new `inline` prop (defaults to `true`),  
- emits a `bx--link--inline` class when `inline` is true,  
- leaves the old API exactly the same (all existing stories and usages will now be underlined by default).

